---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import registry from '../data/affiliates.json';
const paying = registry.vendors.filter((v) => v.status === 'approved');
---
<Base title="Affiliate disclosure" description="Which vendors pay ReceptionistMatch a commission, how much, and how we keep that from deciding what you read.">
<div class="page prose">
  <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
  <p>ReceptionistMatch is free to read. We make money when you sign up for some services through our links. You pay the same price either way.</p>

  <h2>Who pays us</h2>
  {paying.length === 0 ? <p>No vendor pays us yet.</p> : (
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Vendor</th><th>What we earn</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{paying.map((v) => <tr><td>{v.name}</td><td>{v.payout} of what you pay them</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  )}
  <p>Any vendor not in that table pays us nothing. We still list it whenever it fits your business. This table updates as programs approve or end us.</p>

  <h2>How we keep it from deciding the order</h2>
  <p>Rankings and match quiz results are worked out from fit alone: your trade, call volume, hours covered, AI or live people, and budget. Payout is never an input. Affiliate links are marked as sponsored for search engines.</p>
  <h2>What we measure</h2>
  <p>We use Google Analytics to count visits and see which vendor links get clicked. It sets cookies but never collects your name, email or phone number. Any ad blocker or your browser's privacy settings will turn it off.</p>
  <p>Questions? <a href="mailto:hello@receptionistmatch.com">hello@receptionistmatch.com</a>.</p>
</div>
</Base>
